From 5069928246f9d6891d1697394953e020814608be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:38:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Close reliability gaps: sync retry, error monitoring, storage
 detection, backend docs, CI

- esc(): escape single quotes too, closing a latent XSS gap in unquoted-attribute contexts
- Consolidate duplicate error tracking (_fatLog vs db.errorLog) into one source, rehydrate
  it across sessions, and forward errors to a new (documented, unimplemented) error_logs
  table with per-session throttling
- Retry failed cloud sync with exponential backoff, actually resync on the 'online' event
  (it previously only repainted the banner), and let users tap the sync dot to retry now
- Distinguish "device offline" from "Supabase unreachable" with a dedicated health check
  and banner, instead of silently leaving the sync dot red
- Prefer navigator.storage.estimate() for storage-full detection, falling back to the
  existing string-length heuristics where the API is unavailable
- Retry the daily cloud backup on reconnect, not just on load/hourly tick
- Document the inferred Supabase schema/RLS/RPC contracts as reviewable SQL under
  supabase/ (never executed against any live project), plus a new daily-backup Edge
  Function + pg_cron schedule so backups don't depend on the app being opened
- Add a syntax-check tool, a Playwright smoke test, and a GitHub Actions CI workflow

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012zeTdU5zA7jB8uLe97R6yx
